CASE = {'id': 'I6', 'title': 'Crash recovery, dependency retry and transactional outbox', 'difficulty': 6, 'prompt': "All APIs are synchronous functions in app/store.py using Python stdlib SQLite. Only app/ may change. Paths are str. Each operation must be safe across independent connections, durable on return, and close connections. init(path) is idempotent. enqueue(path,id: str,payload: str,depends_on=None) inserts once; duplicate ids preserve their first payload. claim(path,now: int,ttl: int) returns (id,payload,token) or None, selects lexicographically smallest eligible id atomically and increments that job's persistent integer token from 0. ttl<=0 raises ValueError before mutation. Claim transitions pending or expired running jobs to running, sets lease_until=now+ttl, increments attempts. Expiry is lease_until<=now. complete(path,id,token,result: str,now,fault=None)->bool succeeds only for running job with exact token and lease_until>now; stores result and done, clears lease_until. Stale/expired/missing completion returns False without mutation. inspect(path,id)->dict|None returns all columns. Exact jobs schema: id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,payload TEXT NOT NULL,state TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'pending',token INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,lease_until INTEGER,attempts INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,depends_on TEXT,result TEXT. No wall clock: use supplied now. Values are bound SQL parameters. Multiple clients may race; each job must have only one current lease. Tokens fence older claimants even after reopening. No external dependencies. Extend the queue with persistence, dependencies, retry and atomic event publication. A job with depends_on is eligible only after that referenced job exists and is done; missing parents block and cycles remain blocked (no cycle rejection required). retry(path,id,token,now)->bool releases a currently valid running lease to pending, clears lease_until and preserves attempts/token, otherwise returns False; the next claim increments token/attempts. init also creates exact tables outbox(id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,body TEXT NOT NULL,delivered INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0) and inbox(id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,body TEXT NOT NULL). complete must atomically commit done/result and exactly one outbox event (job id and result). Inside that transaction call fault('after_result') after updating job but before inserting event and fault('before_commit') after inserting event but before commit. Propagate hook exceptions and roll back; an actual process crash at either hook must leave neither a completed result nor an event after reopening. A stale completion must not invoke hooks or insert events. publish(path,deliver)->int reads undelivered outbox rows ordered by id, calls deliver(id,body), then durably marks each delivered after callback success, and returns number delivered by this call. On callback error propagate and stop; preserve all already acknowledged deliveries, leave current/unprocessed rows for replay. Publisher calls are sequential (no concurrent publishers required). At-least-once delivery means callback may have applied its side effect before raising/crashing. consume(path,id,body)->bool inserts inbox only once atomically, returns True for first delivery, False for duplicates, preserving first body. Callback may call consume on same DB, so release read transaction/locks before invoking it. Do not automatically publish inside complete. No migration from another schema required. Reopening init must preserve all data. No autonomous retry limits: leases expire and retry is explicit.", 'starter': {'app/__init__.py': '', 'app/store.py': 'import sqlite3\n\ndef init(path):\n    with sqlite3.connect(path) as c:\n        c.execute("CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS jobs(id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,payload TEXT NOT NULL,state TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT \'pending\',token INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,lease_until INTEGER,attempts INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,depends_on TEXT,result TEXT)")\ndef enqueue(path,id,payload,depends_on=None):\n    with sqlite3.connect(path) as c:c.execute(\'INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs(id,payload,depends_on) VALUES(?,?,?)\',(id,payload,depends_on))\ndef claim(path,now,ttl):return None\ndef complete(path,id,token,result,now,fault=None):return False\ndef inspect(path,id):\n    with sqlite3.connect(path) as c:\n        c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row;r=c.execute(\'SELECT * FROM jobs WHERE id=?\',(id,)).fetchone();return dict(r) if r else None\ndef retry(path,id,token,now):return False\ndef publish(path,deliver):return 0\ndef consume(path,id,body):return False\n', 'test_public.py': "import os,tempfile,unittest\nfrom app.store import init,enqueue,claim\nclass PublicTests(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_basic(self):\n        with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as d:\n            p=os.path.join(d,'db');init(p);enqueue(p,'a','work');self.assertEqual(claim(p,0,10),('a','work',1))\n"}, 'reference': {'app/store.py': 'import sqlite3\n\ndef _connect(path):\n    c=sqlite3.connect(path,timeout=10)\n    c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\n    return c\n\ndef init(path):\n    c=_connect(path)\n    try:\n        c.execute("CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS jobs(id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,payload TEXT NOT NULL,state TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT \'pending\',token INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,lease_until INTEGER,attempts INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,depends_on TEXT,result TEXT)")\n        c.execute(\'CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS outbox(id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,body TEXT NOT NULL,delivered INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0)\')\n        c.execute(\'CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS inbox(id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,body TEXT NOT NULL)\')\n        c.commit()\n    finally:c.close()\n\ndef enqueue(path,id,payload,depends_on=None):\n    c=_connect(path)\n    try:\n        with c:\n            c.execute(\'INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs(id,payload,depends_on) VALUES(?,?,?)\',(id,payload,depends_on))\n    finally:c.close()\n\ndef claim(path,now,ttl):\n    if ttl<=0:raise ValueError(\'ttl must be positive\')\n    c=_connect(path)\n    try:\n        c.execute(\'BEGIN IMMEDIATE\')\n        row=c.execute("SELECT j.* FROM jobs j WHERE (j.state=\'pending\' OR (j.state=\'running\' AND j.lease_until<=?)) AND (j.depends_on IS NULL OR EXISTS(SELECT 1 FROM jobs p WHERE p.id=j.depends_on AND p.state=\'done\')) ORDER BY j.id LIMIT 1",(now,)).fetchone()\n        if row is None:c.rollback();return None\n        token=row[\'token\']+1\n        c.execute("UPDATE jobs SET state=\'running\',token=?,lease_until=?,attempts=attempts+1 WHERE id=?",(token,now+ttl,row[\'id\']))\n        c.commit()\n        return (row[\'id\'],row[\'payload\'],token)\n    except BaseException:c.rollback();raise\n    finally:c.close()\n\ndef inspect(path,id):\n    c=_connect(path)\n    try:\n        row=c.execute(\'SELECT * FROM jobs WHERE id=?\',(id,)).fetchone()\n        return dict(row) if row else None\n    finally:c.close()\n\ndef complete(path,id,token,result,now,fault=None):\n    c=_connect(path)\n    try:\n        c.execute(\'BEGIN IMMEDIATE\')\n        row=c.execute("SELECT * FROM jobs WHERE id=? AND state=\'running\' AND token=? AND lease_until>?",(id,token,now)).fetchone()\n        if row is None:c.rollback();return False\n        c.execute("UPDATE jobs SET state=\'done\',result=?,lease_until=NULL WHERE id=?",(result,id))\n        if fault:fault(\'after_result\')\n        c.execute(\'INSERT INTO outbox(id,body) VALUES(?,?)\',(id,result))\n        if fault:fault(\'before_commit\')\n        c.commit();return True\n    except BaseException:c.rollback();raise\n    finally:c.close()\n\ndef retry(path,id,token,now):\n    c=_connect(path)\n    try:\n        with c:\n            n=c.execute("UPDATE jobs SET state=\'pending\',lease_until=NULL WHERE id=? AND token=? AND state=\'running\' AND lease_until>?",(id,token,now)).rowcount\n        return n==1\n    finally:c.close()\n\ndef publish(path,deliver):\n    c=_connect(path)\n    try:\n        rows=c.execute(\'SELECT id,body FROM outbox WHERE delivered=0 ORDER BY id\').fetchall()\n        for row in rows:\n            deliver(row[\'id\'],row[\'body\'])\n            with c:c.execute(\'UPDATE outbox SET delivered=1 WHERE id=?\',(row[\'id\'],))\n        return len(rows)\n    finally:c.close()\n\ndef consume(path,id,body):\n    c=_connect(path)\n    try:\n        with c:n=c.execute(\'INSERT OR IGNORE INTO inbox(id,body) VALUES(?,?)\',(id,body)).rowcount\n        return n==1\n    finally:c.close()\n'}, 'private_tests': {'test_private.py': 'import os,sqlite3,tempfile,unittest\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\nfrom threading import Barrier\nfrom app.store import *\nclass QueueTests(unittest.TestCase):\n    def setUp(self):\n        self.tmp=tempfile.TemporaryDirectory();self.addCleanup(self.tmp.cleanup);self.p=os.path.join(self.tmp.name,\'db\');init(self.p)\n    def add(self,id=\'a\',payload=\'data\',dep=None):enqueue(self.p,id,payload,dep)\n    def test_claim_and_complete(self):\n        self.add();self.assertEqual(claim(self.p,10,5),(\'a\',\'data\',1));self.assertTrue(complete(self.p,\'a\',1,\'ok\',14));r=inspect(self.p,\'a\');self.assertEqual((r[\'state\'],r[\'result\'],r[\'lease_until\']),(\'done\',\'ok\',None))\n    def test_duplicate_preserves_payload(self):\n        self.add();self.add(payload=\'changed\');self.assertEqual(claim(self.p,0,5),(\'a\',\'data\',1))\n    def test_order(self):\n        self.add(\'z\');self.add(\'b\');self.assertEqual(claim(self.p,0,5)[0],\'b\')\n    def test_expiry_boundary(self):\n        self.add();claim(self.p,10,5);self.assertIsNone(claim(self.p,14,5));self.assertEqual(claim(self.p,15,5),(\'a\',\'data\',2))\n    def test_expired_cannot_complete(self):\n        self.add();claim(self.p,0,5);self.assertFalse(complete(self.p,\'a\',1,\'bad\',5));self.assertEqual(inspect(self.p,\'a\')[\'state\'],\'running\')\n    def test_stale_fencing_after_reopen(self):\n        self.add();claim(self.p,0,5);init(self.p);claim(self.p,5,5);self.assertFalse(complete(self.p,\'a\',1,\'bad\',6));self.assertTrue(complete(self.p,\'a\',2,\'good\',6));self.assertEqual(inspect(self.p,\'a\')[\'attempts\'],2)\n    def test_concurrent_single_job(self):\n        self.add();gate=Barrier(2)\n        def worker(_):gate.wait(timeout=5);return claim(self.p,0,10)\n        with ThreadPoolExecutor(2) as pool:rs=list(pool.map(worker,range(2)))\n        self.assertEqual(sum(r is not None for r in rs),1);self.assertEqual(inspect(self.p,\'a\')[\'attempts\'],1)\n    def test_concurrent_distinct_jobs(self):\n        self.add(\'a\');self.add(\'b\');gate=Barrier(2)\n        def worker(_):gate.wait(timeout=5);return claim(self.p,0,10)\n        with ThreadPoolExecutor(2) as pool:rs=list(pool.map(worker,range(2)))\n        self.assertEqual({r[0] for r in rs},{\'a\',\'b\'})\n    def test_invalid_ttl(self):\n        self.add()\n        for ttl in (0,-1):\n            with self.assertRaises(ValueError):claim(self.p,0,ttl)\n        self.assertEqual(inspect(self.p,\'a\')[\'attempts\'],0)\n    def test_unknown_and_done(self):\n        self.assertIsNone(inspect(self.p,\'missing\'));self.assertFalse(complete(self.p,\'missing\',1,\'x\',0));self.add();claim(self.p,0,5);complete(self.p,\'a\',1,\'ok\',1);self.assertIsNone(claim(self.p,100,5));self.assertFalse(complete(self.p,\'a\',1,\'new\',1))\n\n    def test_dependencies_and_retry(self):\n        self.add(\'a-child\',\'child\',\'z-parent\');self.assertIsNone(claim(self.p,0,5));self.add(\'z-parent\',\'parent\');self.assertEqual(claim(self.p,0,5)[0],\'z-parent\');self.assertFalse(retry(self.p,\'z-parent\',9,1));self.assertTrue(retry(self.p,\'z-parent\',1,1));self.assertFalse(retry(self.p,\'z-parent\',1,1));self.assertEqual(claim(self.p,1,5),(\'z-parent\',\'parent\',2));self.assertFalse(retry(self.p,\'z-parent\',1,2));self.assertTrue(complete(self.p,\'z-parent\',2,\'ok\',2));self.assertEqual(claim(self.p,2,5)[0],\'a-child\');self.add(\'cycle-x\',\'x\',\'cycle-y\');self.add(\'cycle-y\',\'y\',\'cycle-x\');self.assertIsNone(claim(self.p,2,5))\n    def crash_at(self,point):\n        import subprocess,sys\n        self.add();claim(self.p,0,5)\n        code="import os,sys;from app.store import complete;complete(sys.argv[1],\'a\',1,\'crashed\',1,lambda p: os._exit(73) if p==sys.argv[2] else None)"\n        r=subprocess.run([sys.executable,\'-c\',code,self.p,point],timeout=10,capture_output=True)\n        self.assertEqual(r.returncode,73,r.stderr.decode());init(self.p);row=inspect(self.p,\'a\');self.assertEqual((row[\'state\'],row[\'result\']),(\'running\',None))\n        with sqlite3.connect(self.p) as c:self.assertEqual(c.execute(\'SELECT COUNT(*) FROM outbox\').fetchone()[0],0)\n        self.assertEqual(claim(self.p,5,5),(\'a\',\'data\',2));self.assertTrue(complete(self.p,\'a\',2,\'recovered\',6));seen=[];self.assertEqual(publish(self.p,lambda *x:seen.append(x)),1);self.assertEqual(seen,[(\'a\',\'recovered\')]);self.assertEqual(publish(self.p,lambda *x:seen.append(x)),0)\n    def test_process_crash_after_result(self):self.crash_at(\'after_result\')\n    def test_process_crash_before_commit(self):self.crash_at(\'before_commit\')\n    def test_delivery_crash_replay_and_dedupe(self):\n        self.add();claim(self.p,0,5);complete(self.p,\'a\',1,\'ok\',1);seen=[]\n        def first(id,body):\n            seen.append((id,body));self.assertTrue(consume(self.p,id,body));raise RuntimeError(\'delivery lost acknowledgement\')\n        with self.assertRaises(RuntimeError):publish(self.p,first)\n        init(self.p)\n        def again(id,body):seen.append((id,body));self.assertFalse(consume(self.p,id,body))\n        self.assertEqual(publish(self.p,again),1);self.assertEqual(seen,[(\'a\',\'ok\'),(\'a\',\'ok\')]);self.assertEqual(publish(self.p,again),0);self.assertFalse(consume(self.p,\'a\',\'changed\'))\n        with sqlite3.connect(self.p) as c:self.assertEqual(c.execute(\'SELECT * FROM inbox\').fetchall(),[(\'a\',\'ok\')])\n    def test_hook_exception_atomic_and_expired_retry(self):\n        self.add();claim(self.p,0,5);self.assertFalse(retry(self.p,\'a\',1,5));calls=[]\n        def fault(point):\n            calls.append(point)\n            if point==\'before_commit\':raise RuntimeError(\'stop\')\n        with self.assertRaises(RuntimeError):complete(self.p,\'a\',1,\'bad\',1,fault)\n        self.assertEqual(calls,[\'after_result\',\'before_commit\']);self.assertEqual(inspect(self.p,\'a\')[\'state\'],\'running\');self.assertTrue(complete(self.p,\'a\',1,\'ok\',2))\n        with sqlite3.connect(self.p) as c:self.assertEqual(c.execute(\'SELECT * FROM outbox\').fetchall(),[(\'a\',\'ok\',0)])\n\n    def test_ordered_delivery_failure_preserves_previous_ack(self):\n        for id in (\'c\',\'a\',\'b\'):\n            self.add(id,id+\'-payload\')\n            leased=claim(self.p,0,10)\n            self.assertEqual(leased[0],id)\n            self.assertTrue(complete(self.p,id,leased[2],id+\'-result\',1))\n        observed=[]\n        def delivery(id,body):\n            observed.append((id,body))\n            if id==\'b\':raise RuntimeError(\'second event fails\')\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(RuntimeError,\'second event fails\'):\n            publish(self.p,delivery)\n        self.assertEqual(observed,[(\'a\',\'a-result\'),(\'b\',\'b-result\')])\n        init(self.p)\n        with sqlite3.connect(self.p) as c:\n            self.assertEqual(c.execute(\'SELECT id,delivered FROM outbox ORDER BY id\').fetchall(),[(\'a\',1),(\'b\',0),(\'c\',0)])\n        replay=[]\n        self.assertEqual(publish(self.p,lambda id,body:replay.append((id,body))),2)\n        self.assertEqual(replay,[(\'b\',\'b-result\'),(\'c\',\'c-result\')])\n        self.assertEqual(publish(self.p,lambda *args:self.fail(\'already delivered\')),0)\n'}}
